# C2: mlmf-conformance's direct dependencies. Changing this file is a
# deliberate act. Keep sorted.
#
# The two BACKENDS, and that combination is the entire reason this crate
# exists. It is the only place in the workspace where more than one backend
# is linked into one binary, which is what a cross-backend conformance test
# needs and what neither backend may have -- a dependency between two
# sibling backends is not a relationship the seam describes.
#
# mlmf-meta is here for the same reason and not a different one: its corpus
# differential needs mlmf-meta and mlmf-gguf in ONE binary, and
# [dev-dependencies] is refused for every gated member, so the test cannot
# live in mlmf-meta. Putting it in mlmf-gguf instead would make a FORMAT
# crate depend on mlmf-meta, which is the edge C4 exists to refuse. This
# crate is shaped like a consumer, and a consumer is what reaches both.
#
# (This line said "All three" until mlmf-meta made it four. A count in a
# comment has to be EDITED to stay true, and the edit is the step that gets
# skipped -- so it is now a description rather than a tally.)
#
# A missing file here is a loud panic in deps.rs::allow_list rather than a
# trivially-satisfied empty list, which is why this file is written out
# rather than left absent.
mlmf-core
mlmf-gguf
mlmf-meta
mlmf-safetensors
